[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: SatLink-Z7 Software Requirements Specification

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-SYS-001
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Processor partitioning
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall run embedded Linux on Cortex-A9 Core 0, FreeRTOS on Cortex-A9 Core 1 and
bare-metal firmware on a MicroBlaze V soft processor in the PL.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Mirrors a real payload or instrument: a host computer, a hard-real-time controller and a
housekeeping sub-controller.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-SYS-002
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Exclusive resource ownership
STATEMENT: >>>
Every peripheral, PL block, interrupt and DDR region shall have exactly one owner (linux, rtos,
hkc or shared) recorded in the ICD address map.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
AMP systems fail in subtle ways when two operating systems touch the same hardware.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-SYS-003
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Telecommand and telemetry interface
STATEMENT: >>>
The payload shall accept telecommands and deliver telemetry as CCSDS Space Packets using PUS
services over UDP/IP on Ethernet.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Standard space ground interface (ECSS-E-ST-70-41C). Detailed in Stage 5.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-SYS-004
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Instrument control interface
STATEMENT: >>>
The payload shall provide a SCPI command interface on TCP port 5025.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Allows scripted control with pyVISA like a laboratory instrument. Detailed in Stage 6.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-SYS-005
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Adaptive coding and modulation
STATEMENT: >>>
The modem shall switch between MODCODs at frame boundaries based on the measured link quality.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Core function of a software-defined telecom payload. The physical layer supports it from
Stage 4 (the MODCOD is signalled in every frame header); the controller follows in Stage 5.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-BLD-001
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Single build system
STATEMENT: >>>
All software shall build from one CMake project with presets for the host, Linux (Core 0),
FreeRTOS (Core 1) and MicroBlaze V targets.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
One build entry point keeps the four targets consistent and CI simple.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-BLD-002
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Warning-free code
STATEMENT: >>>
SatLink C and C++ code shall compile without warnings using -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic
-Wconversion -Wsign-conversion and -Werror.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Warnings are cheap early defect detection (shift-left).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-BLD-003
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Continuous integration
STATEMENT: >>>
Every push and pull request shall run formatting checks, static analysis, host unit tests,
sanitizer tests, cross builds for all embedded targets and the ICD/traceability consistency
checks.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Defects are found minutes after they are introduced.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-BLD-004
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Static analysis
STATEMENT: >>>
C and C++ code shall be analysed with clang-tidy and cppcheck; a MISRA C:2012 report shall be
produced for the C code on every CI run.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Industry practice for safety-and mission-critical embedded code.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-BLD-005
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Unit test coverage
STATEMENT: >>>
Line coverage of the libraries shall be measured on every CI run and shall be at least 80 %.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Makes test gaps visible and keeps them from growing.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-BLD-006
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Reproducible Linux build
STATEMENT: >>>
The Linux image shall be built with Yocto from a kas configuration that pins all layer
revisions.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Anyone can rebuild the exact image from the repository.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-ICD-001
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Register maps as single source of truth
STATEMENT: >>>
Register maps shall be defined only in the YAML files under icd/regmap; C headers, C++ headers
and ICD documentation shall be generated from them, and CI shall fail if the generated files are
out of date.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Prevents drift between FPGA, firmware, drivers and documentation.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-ICD-002
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Register map validation
STATEMENT: >>>
The generator shall reject misaligned or duplicate register offsets, overlapping fields, fields
outside bits 31..0, unknown access types and reset values with bits outside all fields.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Interface errors are caught before they reach hardware.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-ICD-003
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Address and interrupt map
STATEMENT: >>>
The ICD shall list base address, size, interrupts, owner and status for every PL block and every
PS peripheral used, and the generator shall reject overlapping regions, duplicate interrupts and
unaligned bases.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Device tree, FreeRTOS BSP and MicroBlaze firmware all derive from one table.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-ICD-004
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: AMP memory partitioning
STATEMENT: >>>
The ICD shall define non-overlapping DDR partitions for Linux, FreeRTOS, the IPC shared memory and
modem DMA buffers, all inside physical DDR.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Required for safe AMP operation (Stage 4).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-LIB-001
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: CRC-16-CCITT
STATEMENT: >>>
The common library shall provide CRC-16-CCITT with polynomial 0x1021, initial value 0xFFFF, no
reflection and no final XOR, as used for the CCSDS frame error control field.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Bit-exact reference for the ccsds_frame_accel PL block and for software framing.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-LIB-002
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: CCSDS pseudo-randomizer
STATEMENT: >>>
The common library shall provide the CCSDS 131.0-B pseudo-randomizer with h(x) = x^8 + x^7 + x^5
+ x^3 + 1, seeded with all ones at the start of every frame.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Bit-exact reference for the ccsds_frame_accel PL block.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-LIB-003
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Portable common library
STATEMENT: >>>
The common library shall be written in C11, use no dynamic memory and no operating system
services, and build for all four targets.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The same code runs on Linux, FreeRTOS, the MicroBlaze V and the host test build.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-LIB-004
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: CRC-32
STATEMENT: >>>
The common library shall provide CRC-32 (IEEE 802.3, reflected, initial value and final XOR
0xFFFFFFFF) for firmware image checks, bit-compatible with zlib's crc32().
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Host tools can compute image checksums with standard libraries.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-BSP-001
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Yocto BSP layer
STATEMENT: >>>
A Yocto layer meta-satlink shall provide the machine configuration, image recipe and boot files
for the Zybo Z7-20.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Owning the BSP is part of the project scope.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-BSP-002
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Kernel configuration
STATEMENT: >>>
Kernel configuration changes shall be kept as configuration fragments in meta-satlink; a
PREEMPT_RT fragment shall be selectable with SATLINK_RT = "1".
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Reviewable, minimal kernel configuration changes.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-BSP-003
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Board boot
STATEMENT: >>>
The image shall boot from SD card to a login prompt on the UART1 console and accept SSH
connections over Ethernet.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Stage 1 exit criterion.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-BSP-004
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: QEMU smoke test
STATEMENT: >>>
The kernel, device tree and root file system shall boot to a login prompt in QEMU's
xilinx-zynq-a9 machine, driven by an automated script.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Linux integration can be tested without hardware (shift-left).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-BOOT-001
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Stage 1 boot chain
STATEMENT: >>>
The board shall boot FSBL, bitstream and U-Boot from BOOT.BIN on SD card; U-Boot shall load the
kernel and device tree with a boot script.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Baseline boot chain; hardened in Stage 3.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-BOOT-002
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Secure A/B boot
STATEMENT: >>>
U-Boot shall boot only signed FIT images, keep A and B slots, count boot attempts of a slot on
trial and roll back to the other slot automatically once the boot limit is exceeded. Linux shall
end a trial only after the system reached a healthy state, and shall install updates only into
the slot that is not running.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
An update must never leave the payload unbootable, and an unsigned or corrupted kernel must
never run.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-BOOT-003
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Golden image fallback
STATEMENT: >>>
The SD card shall hold a read-only golden copy of the factory root file system that updates
never modify. U-Boot shall boot it when both slots have failed.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Last line of defence: the payload stays reachable for a new update even after two bad slots.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-DOC-001
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Architecture documentation
STATEMENT: >>>
The architecture shall be documented in arc42 structure with diagrams, and significant decisions
shall be recorded as ADRs.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Makes design intent reviewable.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-DOC-002
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Traceability
STATEMENT: >>>
A traceability matrix linking every requirement to implementing and verifying artifacts shall be
generated from source tags, and CI shall fail on tags that reference unknown requirements.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Requirements, code and tests stay consistent.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-DRV-001
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Platform driver with device-tree binding
STATEMENT: >>>
Each Linux-owned PL block shall have an out-of-tree platform driver matched by a device-tree
compatible string, with its register base, size and interrupts taken only from the device tree,
never hard-coded.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Matches upstream kernel practice and keeps the driver correct if the address map changes.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-DRV-002
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Char device control interface
STATEMENT: >>>
Each platform driver shall expose a character device with an ioctl interface for control and
status registers; ioctl argument structs shall be defined once in a shared UAPI header used by
both the kernel driver and user space.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A single struct definition prevents kernel/user-space layout mismatches.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-DRV-003
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Interrupt-driven status
STATEMENT: >>>
Each platform driver for a block that has an interrupt in the ICD shall request that interrupt
from the device tree and shall not require user space to poll status registers for normal
operation. Blocks without an interrupt expose their status through an ioctl read.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Polling from user space wastes CPU and adds latency; where the hardware raises an IRQ, use it.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-DRV-004
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: DMA through dmaengine
STATEMENT: >>>
Bulk data transfer to and from a Linux-owned PL block shall use the kernel dmaengine API against
the block's dedicated AXI DMA channel; the driver shall not implement its own descriptor rings.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Reuses a reviewed, maintained subsystem instead of a bespoke and harder-to-verify one.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-HAL-001
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: C++ HAL over the char device
STATEMENT: >>>
A C++20 HAL class shall wrap each driver's ioctl interface behind a RAII object with typed
methods, so application and test code never issues raw ioctl() calls.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Keeps ioctl numbers and struct layouts in one place and gives callers a safe, typed API.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-HAL-002
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: HAL testable without hardware
STATEMENT: >>>
Each HAL class shall depend on an abstract char-device-I/O interface, injected at construction,
so host unit tests can exercise HAL logic against a mock with no board present.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Driver logic (sequencing, error mapping, retries) must be verifiable in CI, which has no Zybo
board attached.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-PER-001
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Audio codec configuration from Linux
STATEMENT: >>>
Linux shall configure the SSM2603 audio codec over the PS I2C controller (line-in to ADC, DAC to
headphone out, 48 kHz, I2S slave) through a HAL class that sends register frames over an
abstract I2C bus interface. The HAL shall keep a shadow of the write-only registers.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The codec's data path belongs to the PL modem; Linux only sets it up. The device cannot be read
back, so the driver needs its own record of what it wrote.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-PER-002
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: CAN through SocketCAN
STATEMENT: >>>
PmodCAN #1 (MCP2515 on PS SPI1) shall be exposed as a SocketCAN interface using the mainline
mcp251x driver, described by the device tree, and shall pass a loopback frame test from a script
using can-utils.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Reuses the mainline driver and standard tooling instead of a bespoke CAN stack.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-DIAG-001
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Diagnostic command line tool
STATEMENT: >>>
A command line tool shall exercise the frame accelerator, spectrum tap and codec through the HAL
classes. Its command logic shall be separated from device opening so that host unit tests run it
against mocks.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
First thing to run on a fresh board, and its logic is checked in CI without hardware.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-HKC-001
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Housekeeping controller firmware
STATEMENT: >>>
The MicroBlaze V shall run bare-metal firmware that owns the XADC, the timebase watchdog, the
switches and RGB LED, and PmodCAN #2 through its own MCP2515 driver over AXI Quad SPI. The
MCP2515 driver shall be portable C with the SPI transfer injected, so it is unit-tested against
a register-level model of the chip.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A housekeeping sub-controller independent of Linux, as on real payloads; the CAN driver is
written, not borrowed, and verified without hardware.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-HKC-002
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: CAN bootloader
STATEMENT: >>>
A bootloader in BRAM shall load the housekeeping application over CAN, verify it (transport
CRC, image header and payload CRC, load address and entry point) before it can be started, and
tolerate lost frames and responses without corrupting the image.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Firmware of the sub-controller is updated in the field over the bus it already has.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-HKC-003
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Housekeeping CAN protocol
STATEMENT: >>>
Housekeeping telemetry (temperature, supply voltages, status), commands with acknowledgements
and time synchronisation shall be exchanged over CAN at 500 kbit/s with 11-bit identifiers,
defined once in a portable C library used by the firmware and by Linux.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
One definition on both ends of the bus.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-HKC-004
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Firmware image format
STATEMENT: >>>
Housekeeping application images shall carry a header with magic, load address, entry point,
size, version, payload CRC-32 and header CRC-32; the build shall produce such images and the
bootloader and Linux tools shall check them.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A wrong or damaged image is rejected before it runs.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-HKC-005
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Housekeeping application behaviour
STATEMENT: >>>
The housekeeping application shall send telemetry at a commandable period (100 ms to 10 s,
default 1 s), latch XADC alarms and CAN errors until cleared, blink a heartbeat LED, and enter
the bootloader on a keyed command. Its logic shall be free of register access and unit-tested
on the host.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Predictable, testable behaviour of the sub-controller.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-HKC-006
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Linux housekeeping tool
STATEMENT: >>>
A Linux tool shall monitor housekeeping telemetry, send commands and load application images
over SocketCAN, retrying requests whose response is lost. At boot a service shall load the
application image shipped in the root file system.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Operators and the boot sequence use the same tested client.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-MDM-001
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Forward error correction
STATEMENT: >>>
The modem shall use the CCSDS K = 7 rate 1/2 convolutional code (131.0-B) with the CCSDS
puncturing patterns for rates 2/3, 3/4, 5/6 and 7/8, terminated blocks, and a soft-decision
Viterbi decoder.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Standard space channel code with a well-known performance; soft decisions gain about 2 dB.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-MDM-002
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Modulations and MODCOD table
STATEMENT: >>>
The modem shall support Gray-mapped BPSK, QPSK and 8PSK with unit symbol energy and max-log
soft demapping, combined into at least five MODCODs ordered by spectral efficiency, each with an
Es/N0 threshold.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Range of operating points for adaptive coding and modulation.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-MDM-003
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Pulse shaping
STATEMENT: >>>
Symbols shall be shaped with a root-raised-cosine filter (roll-off 0.35, span 8 symbols, unit
energy); the software model shall provide the taps for the PL filters and for simulation.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Band-limited signal without inter-symbol interference after matched filtering.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-MDM-004
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Physical-layer frame
STATEMENT: >>>
Every frame shall start with the CCSDS ASM (BPSK) and a CRC-protected, repetition-coded BPSK
header that announces MODCOD, frame type and sequence number, followed by a randomized,
CRC-16-protected, FEC-coded 128-byte payload with pilot blocks every 512 payload symbols.
Without data the transmitter shall send idle frames with a known PN9 payload.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The receiver learns each frame's MODCOD before its payload arrives (frame-by-frame ACM), and idle
frames give a continuous bit error rate measurement.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-MDM-005
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Receiver performance
STATEMENT: >>>
The receiver shall acquire and track symbol timing, frame timing and carrier phase from an
unknown start, decode at least 22 of 25 frames of each MODCOD at 1 dB above its Es/N0 threshold
in AWGN, and estimate Es/N0 within 1.5 dB.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Verifiable link performance; the Es/N0 estimate drives ACM.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-MDM-006
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Channel model
STATEMENT: >>>
A seeded channel model shall apply gain, carrier phase and frequency offset, fractional timing
offset and complex AWGN at a given Es/N0.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Reproducible link tests without hardware; the same model drives the software loopback.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-MDM-007
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Modem application
STATEMENT: >>>
The Core 1 modem application shall accept configuration, channel, ACM, time and TX frame
messages, queue TX frames, send idle frames when the queue is empty, forward received data
frames, report status once per second, and run a software loopback when the PL datapath is not
used. It shall contain no OS or register access.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The same code runs in the firmware, in the payload simulator and in unit tests.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-AMP-001
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: FreeRTOS firmware on Core 1
STATEMENT: >>>
Linux shall load the FreeRTOS modem firmware from the root file system into the rtos_fw
partition, start it on Cortex-A9 Core 1 and see it report RUNNING within 2 s. The firmware shall
not initialise resources Linux owns (L2 cache controller, SCU, GIC distributor).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Hard-real-time modem control beside a general-purpose OS on one chip.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-AMP-002
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Inter-core message rings
STATEMENT: >>>
Linux and the firmware shall exchange messages through two lock-free single-producer /
single-consumer rings in the shared partition, with interrupt doorbells in both directions. The
ring implementation shall be one source file used by the kernel driver, the firmware and the
host tests.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No drift between the two sides of the protocol; the transport is testable on the host.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-AMP-003
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Message set and Linux interface
STATEMENT: >>>
The message set between Linux and the firmware shall be defined once in a C library with
encoders and decoders; Linux user space shall use it through a character device and a typed C++
client.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
One definition of every message; applications never handle raw bytes.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-AMP-004
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Memory isolation
STATEMENT: >>>
Linux shall reserve every DDR region Core 1 owns as no-map memory, and the firmware's MMU shall
map only the regions and peripherals the address map gives to the RTOS or to both; any other
access from Core 1 shall fault.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A stray pointer on one core must not corrupt the other OS.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-AMP-005
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Firmware fault detection and recovery
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall report aborts, failed assertions, stack overflows and heap exhaustion in the
shared control block and keep a heartbeat; Linux shall restart Core 1 after a fault report or a
heartbeat stalled for 3 s.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
FDIR: the modem recovers without a reboot of the payload.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-AMP-006
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Modem DMA streams
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall stream TX symbols to and RX samples from the PL through the AXI DMA in
scatter-gather mode with interrupt-driven descriptor rings, count underruns and overruns, and
keep descriptors and buffers in non-cacheable memory.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Continuous real-time streams without CPU copies of every sample and without cache maintenance.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SRS-AMP-007
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: AMP testable without hardware
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall run a self-test through its own IPC rings when no Linux is present, and CI
shall boot it in QEMU's Zynq-7000 machine; a simulated Core 1 running the modem application
shall be available to Linux-side software on the host.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The port, scheduler, MMU, interrupts and IPC are verified on every push, not only on the board.
<<<
